;; What this case exercises; edit by hand.  `bb corpus-accept' leaves it alone.
(:book "Aligment of Paragraphs in Bilingual Texts"
 :source "Aligment of Paragraphs in Bilingual Texts.pdf"
 :page 5
 :exercises "A paper numbering the sections its outline names bare, at two
depths on one page: \"3 Distance Measure\" with \"3.1 Baseline
Distance Measure\" and \"3.2 Proposed Distance Measure\" under it.
The title match has to read each title behind its number, and the
heading keeps the number the page wrote - papers cite sections by it.
Captured red: all three headings stacked at the page top, the
children above their parent, both of them folding to nothing while
the real section lines read as prose.  The display equations and the
algorithm steps make the page's shape, and none of them may take a
heading."
 :budget (:mid-sentence 0 :glued 0))
